{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1101107-vampire-taking-a-beats-from-damage","id":1101107,"title":"Vampire taking a beats from damage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-06T22:06:33-07:00","id":1101107,"title":"Vampire taking a beats from damage","content":"So, in Chronicles of Darkness we have this guideline for beats:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">&gt; If your character takes damage in one of her three rightmost Health boxes, take a Beat.<br /> <br /> In Requiem, we have this:</span><br /> <br /> &gt; <span style=\"font-family:arial\">If your character takes lethal damage in one of her rightmost Health boxes, take a Beat. Vampires do not gain Beats from bashing damage.</span><br /> <br /> Understandably, vampires are tougher enemies, so it makes sense that they would only take beats from lethal damage. However, the amount of damage seems a bit harsh, considering<br /> <br /> &gt; At the end of a vampire\u2019s turn, after any reflexive healing, if her last (rightmost) Health box is filled with lethal damage, she falls to torpor.<br /> <br /> And also<br /> <br /> &gt; Kindred take only bashing damage from many sources that would normally cause lethal damage to humans.<br /> &gt; Those few terrible things that cause aggravated wounds to mortals cause only lethal harm to vampires.<br /> <br /> So under most situations (fights not involving sunlight, fire, etc., just normal weapons), in order for a vampire to gain a beat, they have to first lose all of their health levels in bashing damage, then lose that once more to fill their health bar with lethal damage, and then they either heal themselves before the end of the turn, or they fall into torpor? That would be quite the beating - most likely causing a Detatchment roll for vampires with Humanity 7-6 (and another beat), so would falling into Torpor with Humanity 6.<br /> <br /> Does that seem a bit excessive to anyone? How often does this beat criteria come up in your stories?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12211-thepiachu","name":"ThePiachu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T22:49:07-07:00","id":1101116,"title":"","content":"Note that the Beat criteria says when <i>one of</i> the character's rightmost health <i>boxes</i> is marked with the appropriate type of damage, whereas the rules for Torpor and unconsciousness say when the character's rightmost health <i>box</i> (as in, only the third one) is filled with the appropriate type of damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-07-2017, 01:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T04:06:01-07:00","id":1101169,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's excessive for a character suffered Bashing damage in their rightmost box as a vampire the first time to get a beat. They'd get a beat and a detachment check, as they come to the realization they're MUCH more resilient than before. The same with torpor. The first time they get knocked into torpor (regardless of how) would be a &quot;near death&quot; experience to them.<br /> But I would not allow characters to beat each other with fists, heal themselves, and do it again to farm beats.<br /> That kind of scenario doesn't usually come up though because my players and I think playing a character who persistantly sustains that kind of damage is not conducive to continued game play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 06-07-2017, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T05:07:20-07:00","id":1101175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1101107-vampire-taking-a-beats-from-damage?p=1101169#post1101169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's excessive for a character suffered Bashing damage in their rightmost box as a vampire the first time to get a beat. They'd get a beat and a detachment check, as they come to the realization they're MUCH more resilient than before. The same with torpor. The first time they get knocked into torpor (regardless of how) would be a &amp;quot;near death&amp;quot; experience to them.<br /> But I would not allow characters to beat each other with fists, heal themselves, and do it again to farm beats.<br /> That kind of scenario doesn't usually come up though because my players and I think playing a character who persistantly sustains that kind of damage is not conducive to continued game play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fight Club non-withstanding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T09:43:06-07:00","id":1101269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1101107-vampire-taking-a-beats-from-damage?p=1101116#post1101116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that the Beat criteria says when <i>one of</i> the character's rightmost health <i>boxes</i> is marked with the appropriate type of damage, whereas the rules for Torpor and unconsciousness say when the character's rightmost health <i>box</i> (as in, only the third one) is filled with the appropriate type of damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that makes more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12211-thepiachu","name":"ThePiachu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}